✅ 🔧 Final Code (Fully Commented)
class Solution {
    public String shortestCommonSupersequence(String str1, String str2) {

        int n = str1.length();
        int m = str2.length();

        int dp[][] = new int[n+1][m+1];

        // 🔹 STEP 1: Build LCS table
        // dp[i][j] = LCS length of str1[0...i-1] and str2[0...j-1]
        for(int i = 1; i <= n; i++){
            for(int j = 1; j <= m; j++){

                // ✅ Match case → take diagonal +1
                if(str1.charAt(i-1) == str2.charAt(j-1)){
                    dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j-1] + 1;
                }     
                else{
                    // ❌ Mismatch → take best of UP or LEFT
                    dp[i][j] = Math.max(dp[i-1][j], dp[i][j-1]);
                }
            }
        }

        StringBuilder ans = new StringBuilder();
        int i = n, j = m;

        // 🔹 STEP 2: Build Shortest Common Supersequence (reverse direction)
        while(i > 0 && j > 0){

            // ✅ Same character → include once
            if(str1.charAt(i-1) == str2.charAt(j-1)){
                ans.append(str1.charAt(i-1));
                i--;
                j--;
            }
            // 🔼 UP is better → take from str1
            else if(dp[i-1][j] > dp[i][j-1]){
                ans.append(str1.charAt(i-1));
                i--;
            }
            // ◀️ LEFT is better → take from str2
            else{
                ans.append(str2.charAt(j-1));
                j--;
            }
        }

        // 🔹 STEP 3: Add remaining characters
        while(i > 0){
            ans.append(str1.charAt(i-1));
            i--;
        }

        while(j > 0){
            ans.append(str2.charAt(j-1));
            j--;
        }

        // 🔹 Reverse because we built answer backwards
        return ans.reverse().toString();
    }
}
🧠 Core Logic (Ultra Simple)

👉 Tum LCS build karte ho (common part)
👉 Phir non-common characters add karte ho

🔥 Idea:

SCS = str1 + str2 − LCS overlap

